WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.710
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:05.690
In this lesson, we will set up voice channels for team coordination.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.119
Field teams need the correct channel membership and working device audio

00:00:10.159 --> 00:00:12.170
before an exercise or deployment.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.800
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.659
practical way to check the result.

00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:21.799
A search team uses its team channel during a training exercise.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.340
Coordinate field teams through app-based voice channels.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.510
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.840
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.079
Voice.

00:00:33.459 --> 00:00:35.049
Push-to-Talk voice channels.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.929
Create channels and add the members who use them.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:40.810
Availability also depends on PTT.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.329
Check access in the target department.

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:44.549
Push-to-Talk.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.850
The Push-to-Talk add-on: voice channels in the Resgrid apps.

00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:52.510
Review seats, supported clients and channel setup.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:57.609
PTT does not provide phone dispatch alerts or certify radio replacement.

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:00.379
Availability also depends on PTT.

00:01:00.869 --> 00:01:02.729
Check access in the target department.

00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:06.140
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.310
Step 1.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:10.769
Confirm Push-to-Talk access and supported clients.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:11.939
Step 2.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.370
Create a training channel and add its intended members.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:16.559
Step 3.

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:20.830
Join from two demo devices and verify transmit, receive,

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.299
and microphone permissions.

00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:24.429
Now verify the result.

00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:29.299
Check membership and actual audio in both directions on the devices used.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.509
Review channel access after membership changes.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.480
A common problem to watch for: Push-to-Talk channel setup is

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.070
separate from phone voice alerts and audio-stream configuration.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:42.300
Your practice task is simple.

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:46.379
Run a two-device training-channel check and record which members

00:01:46.379 --> 00:01:47.839
can transmit and receive.

00:01:48.219 --> 00:01:52.120
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

